	<FilterPreset ObjectID="9" ClassID="ee52a7d2-069e-47f7-aa30-e3e3286b65a3" Version="3">
		<Description>Hello! Thank you for purchasing this pack :) Here is a low down of how to use this thing:&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;- Each folder below is for separate project frame rates. 60FPS will be the smoothest looking and most commonly used!&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;- Create an adjustment layer on your project and apply any of these zooms to that adjustment layer ABOVE your footage.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;- OR, apply these zooms to PNG's, JPEGS and other independant components, up to you!!&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;- All of these zooms, zoom into 200 SCALE, you can change this directly yourself by going into the effect controls of the clip where the effect is applied and manually changing the scale value on the last keyframe. &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;- I've included BLANK position keyframes on the end of each zoom, so if you want to zoom left, right or anywhere but the middle, go into effetc controls and customise that last keyframe to where you'd like the zoom to end.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;- Finally, the zoom OUT effect. If you cut your clip where you'd like the zoom OUT to begin, make sure to *REMOVE THE ZOOM IN EFFECT* from that clip, then apply the zoom OUT effect to that. It will zoom out! Once again, like the reverse of the normal zoom in effects, you may need to change the first BLANK keyframes to match where the zoom IN ended on your clip.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Thanks again for being an awesome customer!! &#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;PS: I am aware that pirating and illeagal sharing is common with these packs, and whilst me and the storezar team are cracking down on those who are spreading these links. &#13;&#10;I ask that (if you have aquired these packs that way) you spread the word of these packs and the hard work me and my team put into them. It'd be appreciated.</Description>
		<FilterMatchName>AE.ADBE Geometry2</FilterMatchName>
